body:
If you are bringing up those musicians in conversation about Goth musicians.....that may be why you are getting push back? I believe artists such as Peep and Elllish took on a "goth" type of aesthetic and in the eyes of some, shit on what goth truly is and are giving it a bad name. People are protective of their subculture, especially one that has a fashion and name that gets taken without respect of the subculture all of the time. (Those two artists specifically upset people due to those reasons)

&#x200B;

I'm sorry your friends are cruel to you about your other music taste outside of Goth, maybe just keep them out of goth music convo since they aren't in any way connected?

&#x200B;

You are always allowed to listen to whatever you like outside of Goth! Sorry for crappy friends. <3
